  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\n`open_project` (and the shared `cam.load` script verb) now loads into a fresh app world and replaces the session's document only after loading succeeds. Successful opens clear undo/redo and the previous posted-file metadata. Failed opens preserve the current usable document, history and save destination.\r\n\r\nThis fixes the nonempty-document append bug: reopening a saved Face job no longer duplicates its operations or emits a program that cuts the job twice. There is no project-format/schema, units, post-dialect, dependency or GUI/live-MCP policy change. Live MCP still refuses opening over the user's GUI document.\r\n\r\n## Regression coverage\r\n\r\n`crates/app/tests/mcp_open/mod.rs`, included in the `mcp` test binary:\r\n- `opening_a_saved_job_replaces_operations_and_posts_each_section_once`: imports the box model, creates and generates one Face, confirms the saved file has one cached operation, opens twice over a nonempty document, checks exactly one operation, byte-identical Fanuc output and exactly one section preamble, and verifies cleared undo/redo.\r\n- `opening_an_empty_project_removes_the_old_document_and_redo`: removes old entities/settings and clears both undo and redo, including a bare-save round trip.\r\n- `a_failed_open_preserves_the_document_history_and_save_destination`: missing, malformed, unsupported-version and invalid-unit files preserve the usable job, post output, history and bare-save target.\r\n- `script_load_replaces_the_document_and_forgets_the_previous_post`: pins replacement through the shared script verb and resets stale posted-file metadata.\r\n\r\nThe unchanged product baseline reproduced the duplicate-operation, empty-file replacement and stale-post failures; the failed-open preservation control passed.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nOn the exact head `e5d6553c5c2015ded7e608dcd40163a742594536`, independently executed on Windows:\r\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test mcp --test scripting`: **17 MCP + 18 scripting tests passed**, zero failed/ignored.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\r\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\r\n\r\nThis is the documented targeted manual quick-tier alternative, not a claimed `cargo xtask gate quick` execution. Independent bounded code/document review found no issues. A clean merge preview against current main was checked; later upstream release-only changes do not overlap the patch. Readings: issue #978, the current contribution rules, the project load/validation seam, script Env and GUI/live-MCP document lifecycle.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\nNo GUI/desktop runtime, CNC/control, full batch/release suites or hosted workflow execution. The repository intentionally has no push/PR Actions gates.\r\n\r\nChangelog: MCP open_project and script cam.load replace the current document instead of duplicating operations and posted sections, preserving the old job on failed opens.\r\n\r\nEffort: high (no escalation)\r\n\r\nFixes #978\r\n",
